From 7d153318729c693221cd675fd9d0eff2d4408b6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mira (mira/mira)" <hey2missmira@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 17:36:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] (be) snapshot-remote-unwind pipelined coordinator +
 variant_walk_snapshot hook

Add the `variant_walk_snapshot(int seq, ThreadStackTrace* out)`
declaration to `print_stack_capture.h`. The hook moves the unwind step
out of the handler and into the coordinator. The handler-side
`capture_into_slot` records `(ucontext_t, stack window)` into a
variant-local snapshot ring keyed by `seq & 1`; the coordinator drives
libunwind remote against that snapshot and writes resolved frames into
`*out`. Other variants do not link this hook.

Replace `collect_print_stack`'s body in `print_stack.cpp` with the
pipelined depth-1 coordinator from docs/design/snapshot.md "Coordinator
state machine". One iteration per tid:

  1. SignalBlocked check, no signal sent, no sequence bump.
  2. Read seq, queue the signal. Send failure -> ThreadExited or
     CaptureFailed, sequence bumped.
  3. Pipelined unwind of the previous iteration's pending snapshot.
     Runs while tid_i's handler runs on its thread; reads the opposite
     parity slot (invariant 3 in the design doc), so the next handler's
     write cannot race this read.
  4. Bounded wait for data_ready. Timeout -> Timeout, sequence bumped
     to drain the late handler.
  5. Stage tid_i as pending; bump sequence so the next iteration's
     parity differs.

Final drain unwinds the last pending row outside the pipeline.

`capture_one` is removed: the new collector handles signal + wait +
pipelined walk inline, and capture_one's role (sequential
"send-wait-resolve" per tid) is no longer the shape used here. The
`Defer<>` include drops out with it.

Spec: docs/design/snapshot.md "Multi-threaded interactions",
      "Coordinator state machine".

Co-Authored-By: jover <joverzh@gmail.com>
